# Neo Comp parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoComp
namespace NeoBuzz.Comp
class NeoCompMachine
summary Compressor with four characters (Clean VCA, Glue bus, FET, Opto), knee, lookahead, an external sidechain on input 2 and parallel mix. Use it to control dynamics, glue a bus, or duck a track under a kick.

group Dynamics
Mode        "Mode"          0 3    0    enum Clean Glue FET Opto       | Clean: transparent VCA. Glue: bus VCA. FET: fast feedback. Opto: smooth, program-dependent
    how Chooses the compressor's character: Clean transparent, Glue for buses, FET fast and punchy, Opto slow and smooth.
    sound Clean stays out of the way, Glue binds a mix together, FET adds bite and Opto feels gentle and rounded.
Threshold   "Threshold"     0 1000 700  lin -60 0 dB 1                 | Level where compression starts
    how Sets the level in dB, from -60 to 0, above which the compressor starts turning the signal down.
    sound A lower threshold compresses more of the signal and makes the sound more even and dense.
Ratio       "Ratio"         0 1000 463  ratio 1 20 inf                 | Compression ratio (top: limiting)
    how Sets how strongly signal above the threshold is reduced, from 1:1 up to 20:1 and limiting at the top.
    sound Low ratios are gentle and natural; high ratios flatten the peaks and give a squashed, controlled sound.
Knee        "Knee"          0 1000 250  lin 0 24 dB 1                  | Width of the soft knee
    how Sets how gradually compression sets in around the threshold, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound A wide knee is smooth and hard to notice; a narrow one grabs suddenly and sounds firmer.
Attack      "Attack"        0 1000 639  time 0.00005 0.2               | Time to 63 % of the gain change
    how Sets how fast the gain falls once the signal passes the threshold, from 0.05 ms to 200 ms.
    sound Fast attacks tame transients and dull the punch; slow ones let the hit through before the squeeze.
Release     "Release"       0 1000 532  time 0.005 3                   | Time back to 37 % of the gain change
    how Sets how fast the gain recovers after the signal drops, from 5 ms to 3 s.
    sound Short releases sound lively and can pump; long ones sound smooth and steady.
AutoRelease "Auto release"  0 1    0    switch                         | Program-dependent release: fast after transients, slow under sustained compression
    how Lets the release time follow the material: fast after sharp hits, slow under sustained loud passages.
    sound It sounds more natural and pumps less than a fixed release on mixed material.
group Sidechain
Sidechain   "Sidechain"     0 1    0    enum Internal External         | Detect from the input, or from input 2 (connect a machine to the second input)
    how Chooses whether the compressor listens to its own input or to the machine connected to the second input.
    sound External lets another sound, such as a kick, duck this one for a pumping effect.
ScLowCut    "SC low cut"    0 1000 0    freq 10 500                    | High-pass on the detector: lets the lows through uncompressed
    how Filters the low frequencies, from 10 to 500 Hz, out of the signal the compressor listens to.
    sound Bass no longer triggers heavy squeezing, so the lows stay full while the rest is controlled.
Lookahead   "Lookahead"     0 1000 0    lin 0 5 ms 2                   | Delays the audio so the detector sees peaks coming (adds latency)
    how Delays the audio by up to 5 ms so the compressor sees peaks before they arrive.
    sound Fast peaks are caught cleanly without a click at the start, at the cost of a little latency.
Link        "Stereo link"   0 1000 1000 pct                            | 100 %: both channels get the same gain
    how Sets how much both channels share the same gain reduction, from independent (0 %) to fully linked (100 %).
    sound Linked keeps the stereo image steady; unlinked can widen it but may shift the image on loud one-sided parts.
group Output
Makeup      "Makeup"        0 1000 0    lin 0 24 dB 1                  | Gain after compression
    how Adds 0 to 24 dB of gain after compression.
    sound It brings the level back up after the squeeze, so the compressed sound seems fuller and louder.
AutoMakeup  "Auto makeup"   0 1    0    switch                         | Adds the gain a −12 dBFS signal loses
    how Adds the gain that a -12 dBFS signal loses to compression, automatically.
    sound The level stays about the same as you change Threshold and Ratio, so you hear the character, not the volume.
Character   "Character"     0 1000 0    pct                            | Mode colour: Glue VCA, FET and Opto saturation (Clean ignores it)
    how Sets how strongly the chosen mode adds its own colour: Glue VCA, FET and Opto saturation (Clean ignores it).
    sound More character adds warmth and density to the compressed sound.
Mix         "Mix"           0 1000 1000 pct                            | Dry/wet (parallel compression)
    how Blends the compressed signal with the dry signal.
    sound Mixing some dry back in keeps the punch and detail while adding density, known as parallel compression.
Output      "Output"        0 1000 500  db -24 24                      | Output level
    how Sets the final level in dB, from -24 to +24.
    sound It makes the whole sound louder or quieter without changing its tone.
